# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Witness — environment configuration template
#
# Copy to `.env` and adjust. `.env` is git-ignored and must never be committed.
# In production, do not use .env files — inject via your secret manager. See
# docs/operations/DEPLOYMENT_GUIDE.md.
#
# The defaults below are the SOVEREIGN defaults: nothing here causes an outbound
# connection to any third party. If you change that, you are making a deliberate
# policy decision and it will be logged and surfaced to your users.
#
# This file is organised into three bands, reconciled 2026-09-22 against what the
# running application actually reads (packages/config/src/index.ts is the
# authoritative schema for everything except Neo4j, Casbin and the transcription
# adapter, which read process.env directly — noted where that applies):
#
#   1. ACTIVELY CONSUMED    — the running application reads this today.
#   2. OPTIONAL / DEPLOYMENT-SPECIFIC — consumed when set; safe to leave empty.
#   3. RESERVED — NOT YET CONSUMED — describes planned architecture
#      (OpenSearch, pgvector, NATS, AI extraction) that nothing in the running
#      application reads yet. Setting these has no effect. See the READMEs in
#      services/{ai-orchestrator,consent,identity,ingestion,search} and
#      workers/{extraction,indexing,notification,transcription} for what each
#      one is reserved for.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════


# ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
# │ 1. ACTIVELY CONSUMED                                                        │
# └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

# ─── Deployment profile ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# sovereign  — no external egress permitted (enforced at startup, not advisory)
# hybrid     — external model providers permitted where explicitly configured
# development— local development conveniences enabled; never use in production
WITNESS_DEPLOYMENT_PROFILE=development
WITNESS_INSTANCE_NAME="Local Development"
# Product landing URL (public metadata; distinct from the authenticated app origin).
WITNESS_PUBLIC_URL=http://localhost:3000
NODE_ENV=development
LOG_LEVEL=debug

# Data residency declaration — surfaced to end users in the UI so they can see
# where their words are stored. Free text, e.g. "Australia (ap-southeast-2)".
WITNESS_DATA_RESIDENCY="local development machine"

# ─── Application ports and origins ────────────────────────────────────────────
WITNESS_API_PORT=3001
WITNESS_WEB_PORT=3000
# The browser calls the API directly, so this must be reachable from the browser,
# not from the container. NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefixed values are compiled into the
# client bundle at build time — never put a secret behind this prefix.
#
# Do not point this at a real deployment here. This file is the template every
# service shares; a value changed here changes it for the API, the workers, and
# the web app all at once. If you need the web app specifically to call a real,
# remote API during local development, that is a per-developer choice — make it
# in apps/web/.env.local (git-ignored, copy from apps/web/.env.local.example),
# not here. apps/web/src/lib/runtime-config.ts refuses to start a development
# build against a non-local API URL unless that file's escape hatch is set,
# specifically so a shared .env like this one can never silently become one.
NEXT_PUBLIC_WITNESS_API_URL=http://localhost:3001
NEXT_PUBLIC_WITNESS_PROFILE=development
# Where the web application is served from, when that is not the root of its
# origin — e.g. `/witness`. Compiled into every asset URL at build time.
NEXT_PUBLIC_WITNESS_BASE_PATH=
# The exact browser origin, used for the API's CORS policy. A mismatch is
# refused by the browser before the request reaches Witness.
WITNESS_WEB_ORIGIN=
# Where the API sends a signed-in browser after the OIDC callback. Must be the
# same origin as WITNESS_WEB_ORIGIN; the API refuses to start otherwise.
WITNESS_WEB_BASE_URL=
# Development-only, private-LAN physical-device acceptance testing. Takes
# priority over WITNESS_WEB_ORIGIN above when set; refused outside the
# development profile and restricted to RFC1918 private addresses (see
# packages/config/src/index.ts). Leave empty here — set it in your own
# git-ignored .env, never here, since this file is a committed template and a
# developer's own LAN IP must never become a project default. See
# docs/testing/LIVE_WORKSHOP_ACCEPTANCE_RUNBOOK.md.
WITNESS_DEV_LAN_ORIGIN=

# ─── PostgreSQL — system of record ────────────────────────────────────────────
# The application reads DATABASE_URL only. POSTGRES_HOST/PORT/DB/USER/PASSWORD
# below are consumed by docker-compose (to configure the container), not by the
# application itself — keep them consistent with DATABASE_URL by hand.
POSTGRES_HOST=localhost
POSTGRES_PORT=5432
POSTGRES_DB=witness
POSTGRES_USER=witness
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=change-me-in-every-environment
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://witness:change-me-in-every-environment@localhost:5432/witness?schema=public

# ─── Neo4j — knowledge graph projection (ADR-0011) ─────────────────────────────
# Read directly by services/knowledge-graph and workers/graph-projector's own
# config.ts, not through packages/config. `NEO4J_USER`/`NEO4J_PASSWORD`
# bootstrap the single admin user Neo4j Community Edition supports
# (`NEO4J_AUTH` in docker-compose.yml). The read-only and projector credential
# pairs below are named distinctly for the day this deployment adopts Neo4j
# Enterprise or Apache AGE (open decision D-4/KG-3) and can enforce the
# separation at the database level — until then, both fall back to the admin
# pair, and separation is enforced by which package holds which credential
# (services/knowledge-graph never issues a write query; only
# workers/graph-projector does).
NEO4J_URI=bolt://localhost:7687
NEO4J_USER=neo4j
NEO4J_PASSWORD=change-me-in-every-environment
NEO4J_DATABASE=witness
NEO4J_READONLY_USER=neo4j
NEO4J_READONLY_PASSWORD=change-me-in-every-environment
NEO4J_PROJECTOR_USER=neo4j
NEO4J_PROJECTOR_PASSWORD=change-me-in-every-environment

# ─── Keycloak — identity provider (see ADR-0007) ──────────────────────────────
# KEYCLOAK_ADMIN/KEYCLOAK_ADMIN_PASSWORD/KEYCLOAK_URL/KEYCLOAK_REALM below
# bootstrap the local container and provision the realm import; not read by
# the application at request time (the application reads OIDC_ISSUER and the
# client credentials below).
KEYCLOAK_ADMIN=admin
KEYCLOAK_ADMIN_PASSWORD=change-me-in-every-environment
KEYCLOAK_URL=http://localhost:8080
KEYCLOAK_REALM=witness
KEYCLOAK_CLIENT_ID=witness-api
KEYCLOAK_CLIENT_SECRET=change-me-in-every-environment
OIDC_ISSUER=http://localhost:8080/realms/witness
JWT_AUDIENCE=witness-api
# Where Keycloak (or the development identity-provider double) redirects back
# to after sign-in. Optional — derived from WITNESS_API_PORT if unset.
# WITNESS_OIDC_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:3001/api/v1/auth/callback
# How long a Witness session lasts before it must be renewed (minutes).
WITNESS_SESSION_TTL_MINUTES=480
# Keycloak's own SMTP relay, used for its password-reset/verification email
# (rebranded theme) and reused by Witness's own application-level invitation
# email (services/api-gateway/src/infrastructure/mailer.ts). Production
# values come from the operator secret store; never commit credentials.
# KEYCLOAK_SMTP_HOST=smtp-relay.brevo.com
# KEYCLOAK_SMTP_PORT=2525
# KEYCLOAK_SMTP_FROM=hello@buildwithwitness.com
# KEYCLOAK_SMTP_FROM_DISPLAY_NAME=Witness
# KEYCLOAK_SMTP_REPLY_TO=support@buildwithwitness.com
# KEYCLOAK_SMTP_USER=
# KEYCLOAK_SMTP_PASSWORD=
# KEYCLOAK_SMTP_STARTTLS=true
# KEYCLOAK_SMTP_SSL=false

# ─── Authorisation ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Read by services/api-gateway/src/authz/policy-engine.service.ts.
CASBIN_MODEL_PATH=./packages/policy/model.conf
# Deny-by-default is not configurable. This is here to be explicit about it —
# not read by the application; the code path simply has no other effect.
AUTHZ_DEFAULT_EFFECT=deny

# ─── Transcription ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Read by services/api-gateway/src/transcription/local-whisper.adapter.ts — a
# local CLI binary, not an HTTP endpoint. Diarisation is not implemented
# (STATUS.md: "Speaker diarisation — Deferred"); there is no corresponding
# variable to set.
# WITNESS_WHISPER_BIN=/usr/local/bin/whisper-cli
# WITNESS_WHISPER_MODEL_PATH=/opt/whisper/ggml-base.bin
# WITNESS_WHISPER_MODEL=base

# ─── Limits ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Caps one evidence attachment (audio, document or image); multer enforces it
# before the bytes reach the database.
WITNESS_MAX_EVIDENCE_ATTACHMENT_MB=200


# ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
# │ 2. OPTIONAL / DEPLOYMENT-SPECIFIC — consumed when set                       │
# └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

# ─── MinIO / S3 — evidence object storage ─────────────────────────────────────
# Optional: leave S3_ENDPOINT empty to use Postgres-inline storage instead
# (StoragePort's other adapter, and the sovereign profile's default — verify
# which mode a given deployment actually runs; this is not self-evident from
# the environment alone, see architecture/DATA_MODEL.md §4). A non-empty
# S3_ENDPOINT/S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID while WITNESS_DEPLOYMENT_PROFILE=sovereign is a
# startup error, by design (ADR-0009 — recordings and documents are
# institutional content too, not just AI inference).
S3_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:9000
S3_REGION=us-east-1
S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=witness
S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=change-me-in-every-environment
S3_BUCKET_MEDIA=witness-media
S3_BUCKET_DOCUMENTS=witness-documents
S3_FORCE_PATH_STYLE=true
S3_SERVER_SIDE_ENCRYPTION=AES256
# Per-tenant opt-in is additionally required; this flag alone does not enable egress.
ALLOW_OBJECT_STORAGE_EGRESS=false

# ─── Local AI — summarisation drafting (see ADR-0009) ─────────────────────────
# Default: runs locally via Ollama. No data leaves the boundary. This is NOT
# the extraction pipeline (reserved, band 3 below) — this is the local model
# used for session-summary drafting a human then edits and confirms.
WITNESS_LOCAL_LLM_URL=http://ollama:11434
WITNESS_LOCAL_LLM_MODEL=qwen2.5:1.5b
WITNESS_LOCAL_INFERENCE_CONCURRENCY=2

# External model providers. Leave EMPTY in the sovereign profile — a non-empty
# value here while WITNESS_DEPLOYMENT_PROFILE=sovereign is a startup error.
EXTERNAL_MODEL_PROVIDER=
EXTERNAL_MODEL_API_KEY=
EXTERNAL_MODEL_BASE_URL=
# Per-tenant opt-in is additionally required; this flag alone does not enable egress.
ALLOW_EXTERNAL_MODEL_EGRESS=false

# ─── Billing profile (manual/bank-transfer settlement) ────────────────────────
# Placeholders only. Real values must be supplied through deployment secrets
# and are shown only on authenticated invoice/payment pages. If any one field
# below is set, the whole block becomes required (packages/config validates
# this) — either configure billing fully or leave every field empty.
# BILLING_LEGAL_NAME=
# BILLING_BUSINESS_IDENTIFIER=
# BILLING_ADDRESS=
# BILLING_EMAIL=
# BILLING_BANK_ACCOUNT_NAME=
# BILLING_BANK_BSB=
# BILLING_BANK_ACCOUNT_NUMBER=
# BILLING_PAYMENT_INSTRUCTIONS=

# ─── Deployed pilot — hostnames and TLS ───────────────────────────────────────
# Only used by deployments/cloud-managed/docker-compose.pilot.yml. Names, never
# secrets: the domain is the operator's, and certificates come from Caddy/ACME.
# WITNESS_WEB_HOST=pilot.example.org
# WITNESS_API_HOST=api.pilot.example.org
# WITNESS_OIDC_HOST=id.pilot.example.org
# OIDC_PUBLIC_URL=https://id.pilot.example.org
# WITNESS_ACME_EMAIL=operations@example.org
# Keycloak's own database, separate from Witness's.
# KEYCLOAK_DB=keycloak
# KEYCLOAK_DB_USER=keycloak
# KEYCLOAK_DB_PASSWORD=
# WITNESS_REALM_SEED_PASSWORD=

# ─── First run — bootstrap and invitations (operator scripts) ─────────────────
# `pnpm bootstrap` creates the first organisation and invites its first
# administrator — deny-by-default means no HTTP request can do this, so it is
# the one operation performed outside the application. Refuses to run once any
# organisation exists.
# WITNESS_BOOTSTRAP_ORGANISATION_NAME="Your Institution"
# WITNESS_BOOTSTRAP_ADMIN_EMAIL=
# WITNESS_BOOTSTRAP_ADMIN_NAME=
#
# `pnpm invite` adds a colleague to an existing organisation from the
# operator's terminal. The account is inert until that person signs in
# through the identity provider with a *verified* email that matches.
# WITNESS_INVITE_ORGANISATION="Your Institution"
# WITNESS_INVITE_EMAIL=
# WITNESS_INVITE_NAME=
# WITNESS_INVITE_ROLE=contributor

# ─── Cloudflare Email Routing (operator/CI utility) ───────────────────────────
# Consumed by scripts/cloudflare/*.ts and .github/workflows/cloudflare-email-routing.yml.
# Leave empty in this template. Supply through the operator environment or
# GitHub encrypted secrets; never place production credentials here.
CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=
CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=
CLOUDFLARE_ZONE_ID=
WITNESS_EMAIL_ROUTING_DESTINATION=

# ─── Cloudflare Tunnel (deployments/cloud-managed/docker-compose.pilot.yml) ───
# Used by the `cloudflare` compose profile. The connector dials out, so the
# host needs no public IP and no open port.
# `cloudflared tunnel create witness-pilot` prints the id and writes the
# credentials file. That file is a secret: mount it, never commit it.
# CLOUDFLARE_TUNNEL_ID=

# ─── Observability — local development only ───────────────────────────────────
# Wired into infrastructure/docker/docker-compose.observability.yml (`make
# dev-obs`), not deployed to the production pilot today (STATUS.md).
GRAFANA_ADMIN=admin
GRAFANA_ADMIN_PASSWORD=change-me-in-every-environment
OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:4318
OTEL_SERVICE_NAME=witness
OTEL_TRACES_SAMPLER=parentbased_traceidratio
OTEL_TRACES_SAMPLER_ARG=0.1
# Telemetry NEVER leaves your infrastructure. There is no upstream collector
# and we will not add one. See docs/governance/DIGITAL_SOVEREIGNTY.md.
TELEMETRY_EXTERNAL_REPORTING=false


# ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
# │ 3. RESERVED — NOT YET CONSUMED                                              │
# │    Nothing in the running application reads these. Setting them has no      │
# │    effect. They describe planned architecture — see services/search,        │
# │    workers/{extraction,indexing}, packages/observability's READMEs.         │
# └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

# ─── OpenSearch — planned lexical search projection (services/search) ────────
# The container itself is part of the base compose stack (infrastructure/docker)
# and requires OPENSEARCH_PASSWORD to start — that is a docker-compose
# requirement, not evidence the application reads it: no application code
# queries OpenSearch today (services/search is a reserved scaffold).
OPENSEARCH_NODE=http://localhost:9200
OPENSEARCH_USER=admin
OPENSEARCH_PASSWORD=change-me-in-every-environment
OPENSEARCH_INDEX_PREFIX=witness

# ─── Redis — planned cache/rate-limiting/job coordination ─────────────────────
# Nothing in the application reads REDIS_URL today; rate limiting and session
# handling do not use Redis in the current implementation.
# REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379
# REDIS_KEY_PREFIX=witness

# ─── NATS JetStream — planned event transport (see ADR-0005) ──────────────────
# The current event/projection mechanism is a transactional Postgres outbox
# polled by workers/graph-projector (architecture/DATA_MODEL.md §3, "Event
# log"), not NATS.
# NATS_URL=nats://localhost:4222
# NATS_STREAM_PREFIX=WITNESS

# ─── AI extraction platform — planned (services/ai-orchestrator, workers/extraction) ──
# No AI-assisted knowledge extraction runs anywhere in Witness today. These
# name a planned LiteLLM-fronted extraction pipeline, distinct from the real,
# already-consumed WITNESS_LOCAL_LLM_* summarisation config in band 2 above.
# LITELLM_BASE_URL=http://localhost:4000
# LITELLM_MASTER_KEY=change-me-in-every-environment
# OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434
# MODEL_EXTRACTION=ollama/llama3.3:70b-instruct
# MODEL_SUMMARISATION=ollama/llama3.3:70b-instruct
# MODEL_EMBEDDING=ollama/bge-m3
# EMBEDDING_DIMENSIONS=1024

# ─── Diarisation — planned (workers/transcription) ─────────────────────────────
# DIARISATION_ENABLED=true
# Comma-separated ISO-639-1 codes, or `auto` — planned, not read today.
# TRANSCRIPTION_LANGUAGES=auto

# ─── Consent & retention policy tuning — planned ───────────────────────────────
# Consent enforcement itself is real (see services/consent's README) and is a
# structural domain invariant, not an environment toggle — there is no code
# path to process evidence without a valid consent decision, so these
# variables have nothing to tune yet.
# CONSENT_REQUIRED=true
# CONSENT_DEFAULT_EXPIRY_DAYS=1825
# CONSENT_REVOCATION_SLO_SECONDS=300
# RETENTION_DEFAULT_DAYS=3650
# RETENTION_MEDIA_DAYS=1825

# ─── Graph/search limits — planned ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# The knowledge graph's real traversal-depth cap (MAX_TRAVERSAL_DEPTH) is a
# hardcoded constant (services/knowledge-graph/src/graph-repository.port.ts),
# not environment-configurable, matching this project's "clamp, never trust a
# caller-supplied depth" convention. Rate limiting is not implemented.
# MAX_GRAPH_TRAVERSAL_DEPTH=6
# MAX_SEARCH_RESULTS=200
# RATE_LIMIT_PER_MINUTE=120
